nodecode-image-studio is a rewrite of phdigital01's phdigital01/imagegen-hermes:

  https://github.com/phdigital01/imagegen-hermes
  commit f00dbf81e3b7c1a821086a508048a93eb5dc12b1
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Paulo Henrique Tavares (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's image generation surface as two Nodecode tools and
one command. The FAL wire is the original's queue (submit to
queue.fal.run/<model> with the key in an Authorization header, poll the
status URL, fetch the response URL, read the images out of the result, keep
the answer on FAL's own host), its prompt/aspect-ratio/num_images body, its
reference images passed as image_url and reference_image_urls, and its
default model fal-ai/flux-2-pro. From vertex_api.py: the generateContent
call with the key in x-goog-api-key, the optional project segment on the
model path, inlineData parts for the reference images, responseModalities
IMAGE with an imageConfig of imageSize and aspectRatio, the four Nano
Banana models and gemini-nano-banana-2.1 as the default, and the finish
reason quoted when a candidate carries no picture. The gallery, the
per-call file naming and the error text (status, the provider's own message,
a hint per status) follow the original's studio.

Left out: the desktop studio (FastAPI routes, the TypeScript frontend and the
bundled desktop plugin), because a Nodecode cell is its tools, its command
and its manual, not a window; the Hermes image_gen provider registration and
the `hermes imagegen` CLI, which the two tools and /image-studio replace; the
prompt builder and the host-LLM prompt writer, since the model calling the
tool already writes the prompt; Magnific (upscale, relight, background
removal) and the Hermes-native providers (OpenAI, xAI, Krea, DeepInfra,
OpenRouter, Nous Portal), which need that harness's registries - FAL and
Vertex AI are the two whose wire is public and small; the spend ledger and
the job queue with cancellation, replaced by one gallery index; and the
FAL upload endpoint the original uses to publish local reference files,
so a FAL reference here is an https URL while Vertex AI also takes local
paths.
